  band (trofeo)") — not from hand-drawn approximation. Path data (including
  the circle/diamond cubic-bezier shapes) is copied as-is; only two
  adaptations were needed for VectorDrawable:
  1. stroke-dasharray "1 5" on the two sparkle accents has no VectorDrawable
     equivalent, so each was resampled into discrete dash segments.
  2. the background wash (paint0) is an elliptical radial gradient (Figma's
     gradientTransform applies a non-uniform scale); VectorDrawable's XML
     gradient only supports a circular radius, so it is approximated with a
     circular one sized to the ellipse's larger axis. It is very low-opacity
     (≤0.18) and reads the same in practice.
-->
